From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kirill <sleeply4cat@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:57:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 21/27] media: qcom: camss: add SM6225

SM6225 has three CSIPHY, CSID and TFE instances. TFE 530 and CSID 530
match the 340 drivers at every offset they use, compared against the
downstream register tables. The CSIPHY differs from QCM2290: its lane
sequence comes from the downstream v1.2.1 table.

A PPI bridge sits between CSIPHY and CSID. Downstream writes 0x70 to
its config register for D-PHY, repeated here without knowing the bits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015ya7ekTBjucpaN4ypc4DaZ
